<title>USA: Millipore Q4 loss after writeoff vs profit.</title>
<headline>Millipore Q4 loss after writeoff vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>BEDFORD, Mass. 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			  1995</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.66   profit	 $0.51</p>
<p> Net loss		  28,473   profit	22,580</p>
<p> Sales		    151,418		  154,984</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  43,284		   44,348</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)  </p>
<p>						Year</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $1.00   profit	 $1.90</p>
<p> Net profit		43,622   profit	85,354</p>
<p> Sales		    618,735		  594,466</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  43,602		   44,985</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: Full name is Millipore Corp.</p>
<p>First Call Q4 mean estimate: $0.52 per share.</p>
<p>The current quarter included a pretax, non-cash charge of $68 million, or $1.21 per share, related to the one-time writeoff of in-process research and development costs associated with the acquisition of the Amicon Bioseparations business completed in the fourth quarter.</p>
<p>The current quarter also includes a special gain of $2.5 million from the sale of equity securities.</p>
